 A server's run is one sum type, `Run` in `internal/run.ts` (idle, launching, starting, running, halting), held by `internal/server.ts` (the lifecycle); its `state` and `running` (the documents, the capabilities, the attempt) are derived from it. `internal/attempt.ts` is one process run: it starts and stops the process and routes its messages.
 
@@ -6,4 +6,4 @@ Which specs exist (plan §2 #70 "Detection", "Not installed", #72): `internal/de
 
 A server's identity (plan §2 #83): every `ServerSpec` and `ServerView` carries a `ServerKey` (brand, `internal/spec.ts` `serverKey`) that does not change with its shown name. Detection builds its specs without a key (`FoundSpec`) and gives each one in its last step, beside the shown name: the tool's name with its project always written out (`oxlint (frontend)`, `TypeScript (repository root)`; the shown name is that text only when two projects use the tool), so a suffix coming or going, tsc ↔ tsgo or installed ↔ not installed keep the key, and Vue's spread copy of TypeScript's spec gets its own (`Vue (web)`). `addedSpecs` keys a hand-added server `added: ` plus its command words, never its numbered name. Phpactor and Intelephense are two tools of one preset: their keys differ (`Phpactor (php)`, `Intelephense (php)`). Start, Stop, Restart and the logs still go by the shown name; the key is what the window's off switches and pins hold.
 
